<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! The Veil-Ladder ~ the record

The veil-ladder law speaks at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/the-veil-ladder`>>; its provisional in-house rulings stand in that meme's `#/rulings`, each open to the operator's overrule until the operator settles it. This record keeps the floor work still owed.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/owed`>>

!! Owed ~ for the kahu road

the last-read replica beneath the fallen floor, by a named gap: a face's workbench replica rests sealed in the vessel's own store, but the lockboxes that deliver its content keys open only through that face's Keyhive identity, and that identity's Archive rests as a face record (`veil-archive-g<PersonaGroup>` on the browser, the `veil-archive` face record on the node) under the face's custody tree, so a burn takes the keys with the tree, and hydration besides answers only a session that wears the bag's face (`session-face-foreign`), which a severed face cannot stand. Keeping what the vessel already decrypted needs a re-file of those records under the vessel's key before the tree leaves (a tree cleared outside the vessel gives that act no moment), or a read-only door at the floor for a severed face's bags, and neither stands; the Hold gesture's choice at the join door; a lit set wider than one face per browser boot (a second face's provider refuses `face-edge-absent` at `faceProviders.lit`), and pins keyed by PersonaGroup so that many faces share one island; the fleet-join door's bind and card asked at the offer, read against a real hearth (built for a leaf: a veil's first fleet offer founds its face inside the offer, by the founding door's own one-boot ask, and the boot that founded for it shows the offer with no second tap; a replay founds nothing, and an offer under a standing face founds nothing new); the draft and personal layers of a floor whose key does not stand (they still ride the faceless binding entries there, and the mount's contract keeps both urls whole); and the arrival URL's move off the query string and the fragment (the relay from the Pronaos descriptor, the floor card and anchor through the carriage door).

<<~/ahu>>

